  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the orchestrator and the contributors, we want the operator's decisions of 2026-11-02 (every UXD row takes its recommendation; M4 = validated legacy parity, M5 = evolutions) applied to the docs, the specs, the boards and the tracker, so that nobody ports an evolution into M1–M4 or loses one that was deferred.\n\n### Scope\n\nDecisions: [#379](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379), last two comments (2026-11-02); `docs/migration/UX-DECISIONS-PENDING.md`.\n\n1. M5 everywhere it is relevant: `docs/ROADMAP.md`, `README.md`, `docs/LOTS.md` (the proposed section becomes applied; the (b) halves of the splits become lots 174 to 183 in a new M5 section; `LOT-163` and `LOT-164` dependencies), `docs/FEATURES.md`, `tooling/roadmap` (M5 membership, a board section).\n2. Each decision recorded in its lot spec, or on its lot issue when the lot has no spec yet.\n3. The splits: one new M5 lot and issue per (b) half.\n4. The small (a) follow-ups of the table, each with its milestone (duplicates checked first).\n5. `docs/migration/UX-DECISIONS-PENDING.md` deleted once every row is recorded (the file says so), references fixed.\n\nNo Swift code.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every UXD-01…25 row is recorded in a spec, an issue or #379.\n- [ ] `docs/LOTS.md`, the boards and the roadmap agree on the M5 membership; CI green.\n- [ ] The decision file is deleted and nothing links to it.\n\n### Claim\n\n/claim cloud/docs-steward\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
